{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mergeRemote","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"into","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ids","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deleted","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"policy","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV","text":"MergePolicy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)","extendedModule":"SwiduxPersistence","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"role":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence0B11CoordinatorCAA0A00A10ObservableRzrlE11mergeRemote4into3ids7deleted6policyyAD5StoreCyxq_G_Shy10Foundation4UUIDVGAqA11MergePolicyVSgtYaF"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mergeRemote","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"into","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"store","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC","text":"Store","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ids","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deleted","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"UUID","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> = [], ","kind":"text"},{"text":"policy","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MergePolicy","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"store","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The live store to reconcile.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"ids","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The identities to re-read. IDs matching no row, and IDs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"belonging to another entity type, are harmless.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"deleted","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Identities known to have been deleted elsewhere."}]}]},{"name":"policy","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Narrows the configured policy for this call only.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The O(k) counterpart to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which re-reads every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row of every registered entity on every tick. Where a sync signal carries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"which","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" identities changed, this spends that knowledge: one batched fetch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"per 500 IDs instead of a full-table scan, and only the named entities are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reconciled. Everything else in state is left exactly as it was.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every guarantee ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" makes holds here. Pending","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes are flushed first; an ID with unflushed local intent — a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drained-but-unflushed write, an un-drained edit, a pending deletion, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write whose save failed, or an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" hold — always wins, and that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not configurable.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A partial read cannot tell a deleted row from one that was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never asked about, so this ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"never","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" infers a deletion. An ID vanishes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only if you name it in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deleted"},{"text":", and only if the resolved policy grants","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/removesMissingEntities","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". Name only what you have positive","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"evidence for — a history tombstone, not an empty fetch. In exchange,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"there is no empty-snapshot guard to work around: this can remove the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last surviving entity, which "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Important"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An ID named in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deleted"},{"text":" that storage ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"still holds"}]},{"text":" is not removed. A live","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row is evidence the deletion was itself undone elsewhere; a tombstone can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be stale.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Deferred-rows-are-re-offered","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Deferred rows are re-offered"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tick may read a row and decline to apply it — an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing"},{"type":"text","text":" hold is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one exemption that leaves no other trace. Those rows are remembered by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identity and re-offered on the next call, on top of whatever "},{"code":"ids","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" names,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a caller does not have to re-queue them against its own signal. That"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matters here because a sync signal is generally not resent and releasing a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hold writes no transaction of its own, so without it a hold would quietly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"become a veto. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeChanges(into:policy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" shares the same debt, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"either path settles what the other deferred. Both discard it when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"container is swapped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Registered "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse:"},{"type":"text","text":" resolvers do not run here — a resolver is handed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the whole table and asked which rows survive, and a subset would have it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"judge a world it cannot see. Duplicate rows are still collapsed on read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and still reported. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapseDuplicates(into:)-(Store)"},{"type":"text","text":" or a full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to reclaim them."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistencecoordinator\/mergeremote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)"},"abstract":[{"text":"Re-hydration restricted to the rows a caller already knows changed.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"title":"EntityDB","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A generic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ModelActor"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads and writes any "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Generic sto